A place that waits on the run queue keeps a deadline made on its lender's time once its own account pays for it.
A thread whose lender gave a long span would wait that long on its own time, however short its own span.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a request is due further ahead than its span
Witness: fuzz lend-span-own-time

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -458,8 +458,6 @@ static void place_settle(struct place *p)
             uint32_t vt = vtime(payer);
             if (joined) {
                 request_renew(p, payer, vt);
-            } else if ((int32_t)(p->deadline - vt) > (int32_t)place_span(payer)) {
-                p->deadline = vt + place_span(payer);
             }
         }
         core->run_stale = true;
